  "prompt_text": "The figure compares two kinds of electronic excitation processes in a crystal by plotting energy versus crystal momentum. In both panels, a blue band with a finite width \\(W\\) is shown, and filled blue circles mark occupied states near an extremum of that band.\n\nIn panel a, the same band is involved throughout: multiple gray curved arrows connect nearby momentum states within the blue band, suggesting intraband motion or scattering across the band’s dispersion. A large vertical arrow labeled \\(\\hbar\\omega\\) emphasizes an energy scale associated with driving the system, while the electrons remain within a single band spread over width \\(W\\).\n\nPanel b shows a different situation, with a blue lower band and a red upper band separated by an energy gap \\(\\Delta\\). A vertical arrow indicates excitation from the lower to the upper band, while a bracket labeled \\(n\\hbar\\omega\\) and a ladder of small arrows suggest a multiphoton process in which several quanta are needed to bridge the gap. Additional curved arrows near the lower band imply accompanying momentum-space motion. Overall, the figure contrasts intraband dynamics in one band with interband excitation across a band gap, highlighting the roles of bandwidth, gap size, and photon energy.",
